  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A solid cylinder of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is wrapped with an inextensible light string and, is placed on a rough inclined plane as shown in the figure. The frictional force acting between the cylinder and the inclined plane is:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0111_4e9c13f6baba.png\" style=\"width: 155px; height: 243px;\" /></p><p>[The coefficient of static friction, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub></math>,&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;]</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0111_32937461c8f4.png\" style=\"width: 151px; height: 247px;\" /></p><p>Let&#39;s take solid cylinder is in equilibrium</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>sin</mi><mn>60</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Solving we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>But limiting friction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#60;</mo></math> required friction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>cos</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>mg</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Hence cylinder will not remain in equilibrium</p><p>Hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo></math> kinetic</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>N</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>cos</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
